-- title:
--   Eichler–Shimura representation attached to a Hecke character
-- statement:
--   Let $M \ge 1$ and let $p$ be a prime; let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain that is a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra, $K$ a field which is the fraction field of $O$ and a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra compatibly with $O$, and assume the image of $p$ in $O$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O$. Write $J_1(M)$ for the group of degree-zero divisor classes of the function field of $X_1(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, equipped with the action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ and with the module structure [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleOneBar M`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L129) over $\mathcal{H} = \mathbb{Z}[x_i : i \in \mathrm{Primes} \sqcup \mathbb{N}]$, whose generators $T_\ell$ and $\langle d\rangle$ are `heckeGenOne` and `diamondGen`; write $T_p J_1(M)$ for the group of sequences $(x_n)$ in $J_1(M)$ with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p\,x_{n+1} = x_n$, and $A_1 =$ `rationalHeckeAlgebraOne` for the $\mathbb{Q}_p$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{Q}_p}(\mathbb{Q}_p \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T_p J_1(M))$ generated by the image of $\mathcal{H}$. The assertion is: for every ring homomorphism $\Lambda : A_1 \to K$ whose restriction to the image of $\mathbb{Z}_p$ in $\mathbb{Q}_p \subseteq A_1$ is the structure map $\mathbb{Z}_p \to K$, there exists a [`GaloisRepAdic O`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16), that is, a finite free $O$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with a homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_O(V)$ which is $\mathfrak{m}_O$-adically continuous (for each $n$ some finite subextension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ has $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak{m}_O^n V$ for all $v$ and all $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise), such that: (i) for every prime $\ell \nmid Mp$ and all $a, d \in O$ with $\Lambda(T_\ell) = a$ and $\Lambda(\langle \ell\rangle)\, d = 1$ in $K$, for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $A$ acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - da\,X + d\ell$; (ii) for every prime $\ell \nmid Mp$, $\rho(\sigma) = 1$ for every $\sigma$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of any valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit; and (iii) there is a surjective $K$-linear map $\pi : K \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T_p J_1(M) \to K \otimes_O V$ intertwining the base change to $K$ of the Galois action on the Tate module with the base change of $\rho$, and sending the base change of the action of each $t \in \mathcal{H}$ on the Tate module to multiplication by $\Lambda$ of the image of $t$ in $A_1$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura construction, over a discrete valuation ring, of the two-dimensional $p$-adic Galois representation attached to a system of eigenvalues of the Hecke and diamond operators in weight two on $\Gamma_1(M)$, retained in the form that exhibits the representation as a Galois- and Hecke-equivariant quotient of the Tate module of the modular Jacobian. It is the source of the representations attached to weight-two eigenforms and of the ordinary-line statements for primitive forms used later in the modularity-lifting argument.
